    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0689" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/5–1446: Circular
                    telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Certain Diplomatic and Consular
                            Officers</hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d507-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-14T08:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1946—8 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On leaving Seoul with USSR deleg May 9 Gen Shtikov remarked he had not
                    communicated with Moscow on decision withdraw from Joint Commission
                    meetings.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d507-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d507-f1-content">
                <p>At Moscow and Nanking.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
